    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 4th with a clear focus on exploiting favorable RHP matchups, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who registers as our strongest play of the day. With a wind-out advantage at his back and a high-leverage leadoff spot against Ginn, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is perfectly positioned to capitalize on his elite speed\u2014a priority for our 5x5 build. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (77.93) and **Kyle Schwarber** (77.21) draw a prime assignment against Giolito. While **Kyle Schwarber** continues to provide high-end power upside, **Trea Turner**\u2019s ability to manipulate the basepaths against a pitcher with a 6.49 xERA creates a massive ceiling for our stolen base and run totals today.\n\nThe strategy remains aggressive against mid-tier arms, but we are keeping a close eye on the floor for our lower-order bats. **Caleb Durbin** (60.30) narrowly holds his spot in the utility role; his efficiency is buoyed by favorable park factors, though we are monitoring the matchup against Rogers, Tr. **Yordan Alvarez** (61.50) serves as our lineup anchor despite a tougher draw against Jared Jones; his elite .454 xwOBA makes him a mandatory start regardless of the SP xERA. Conversely, **Kazuma Okamoto** (46.82) and **Pedro Ramirez** (47.38) represent our \"marginal\" tier. **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a significant test against Sale, where his strong platoon edge is largely neutralized by the pitcher\u2019s skill, limiting his upside today. \n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the depth of the bench against the current active group. While **Junior Caminero** and **Colt Keith** are unavailable due to scheduled off-days, we continue to monitor the progress of **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds**, who remain in the minors and are ineligible for today\u2019s active roster. Consequently, we are leaning heavily on our established leadoff-heavy configuration to mitigate the lack of pinch-hit volatility. We are currently proceeding with all starters as listed, provided no late-breaking weather events shift the park factors for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** or **Pedro Ramirez**.",
